- "The comments from others get to me. Each one of them taken on their own is no big deal. But I hear this kind of stuff a lot from other moms and medical providers and family. Is everyone just trying to say what my deepest fear is? That there's an oncoming train called "misbehaving brat" and its all my fault? Are all of these things just polite euphemisms for "your kid is badly behaved" ? can I do anything about it now? Did I miss the window?" [sr019-0041]
- "I’m at a loss for words. My mom keeps labeling my 10 month old calling her anxiety ridden and stressed out when my mom watches her because she rubs her toes together when she self soothes or touches her hair and ears before falling asleep. What kind of person says this? She has labeled me my entire life and it took me YEARS and becoming a mom of my own to realize how awful I was labeled and thought her interpretation was true. I don’t want the same for my daughter." [sr024-0248]
- "so, we knew it was a possibility but not everytime he asks, i can't help but feel frustrated like he's focusing too much on his development instead of enjoying our son regardless of if he is or isn't delayed." [sr076-0119]
- "Mom of a 7 week old baby boy here! Since my kid was born, my FIL keeps snapping his fingers near my boy's ears to see if my baby can turn his head towards the sound (apparently his kid could do it since birth which is a little questionable given it's a milestone for like 2-3 months old?)." [sr070-0103]
