- "When I share that with other moms or show any kind of pride in my own child, I get met with doubt about whether or not he’s *really* doing those things or *really* eating that much. It’s frustrating to feel like people are trying to insinuate that you’re a liar. No, I’m just freaking proud of my kid 😭 and for us, his parents, who are trying our best to thrive despite feeling like we have no clue what we’re doing." [sr098-0045]
- "Being proud of my kid doesn’t mean yours is behind, or that I’m judging your parenting, or that I think I’m better. I’m in a race with myself - no one else. I’m happy for other people when their kids are thriving, and I’m supporting of people when their kids are struggling. I hate feeling like moms want to be pitted against each other." [sr098-0046]

**But:** The kissing remark was not an explicit criticism, and the parent initially thought little of it. "I shrugged it off initially as I didn’t really think anything of it as he’s my son." [sr063-0036]

