- "my in-laws keep telling me to “get her checked out for autism and adhd because this isn’t normal behavior”." [sr010-0011]
- "I keep repeating this is all the “terrible twos”, which they then try to compare her to my other, more chill kid who is 3. Apparently toddlers are all supposed to be the same. So before I start to believe it, this all sounds like normal two year old behavior, right?" [sr010-0013]
- "Last night Bub had a bad night. Waking every couple of hours. Hard to settle to bed. My partner just... went on this long rant about how she can't believe 1 year on Bub is "still so hard" and "fights her sleep" and "is a terrible sleeper" and on and on and on. It's like she's forgotten that for 2 months straight Bub has been amazing. Even when I point it out she just disagrees with me. Then her tone with Bub is so frustrated (not aggressive just almost... demanding?)." [sr010-0197]
- "But also don't want to turn the I'd into a battle of who does more - that's not my point. How do I get her to objectively see that our girl is actually fucking amazing when it comes to this and one bad night doesn't mean the whole year of sleep has been bad." [sr010-0205]

